{"game": "gunfire-reborn", "language": "english", "appid": 1217060, "month": "2025-07", "window": 2, "start_date": 1751932800, "end_date": 1752623999, "month_true_total": 194, "quota": 5, "returned": 5, "pulled_at": "2026-09-27 01:55:03 UTC", "reviews": [{"recommendationid": "199893693", "author": {"steamid": "76561199043568501", "personaname": "decblake", "persona_status": "online", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/profiles/76561199043568501/", "num_games_owned": 81, "num_reviews": 5, "playtime_forever": 18635, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 18067, "last_played": 1786158584, "avatar": "e4c5e2ab869df41657cb2108f0d01723d0ba7ba7"}, "language": "english", "review": "This game is very fun interesting and hugely replayable. It gets updates fairly frequently and is very reasonably priced at base, and the dlcs are worth it for the content they add. The one thing i haven’t been able to do in this game is play multiplayer. Other than that, the only actual gripe I have with this game is that it lacks a one shot protection mechanic on all characters (think risk of rain 2) because of the fact that once you get to reincarnation levels, almost anything with one shot you, or kill you in a quarter of a second if they fire rapidly. If you stop moving in this game for the shortest time, you are most likely dead unless you had a scroll to protect you, simply getting stuck on a wall or a pebble on the ground is a big enough mistake to kill you and I just don’t like that. My advice is to just stop climbing difficulty’s once you get to reincarnation 4, as after that point your variety of builds becomes limited to still win with the difficulty. But yeah other than that it’s an amazing game with new content added frequently that’s great to come back to for a bunch of runs a month.", "timestamp_created": 1752618627, "timestamp_updated": 1752618627, "voted_up": true, "votes_up": 0, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": 0.5, "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchas